#!/usr/bin/env python3
# backdrop: draws the desktop wallpaper and the swaylock image, Catppuccin Mocha.
#
#   backdrop wallpaper   render the full image per active output, hand it to swaybg
#                        (through sway), then make sure each has its lock image cached
#   backdrop lock-args   print swaylock's `-i output:path` args, one per line,
#                        rendering a lock image first if its cache key changed;
#                        also names every output seen before that is not connected
#                        now, so one docked while locked gets its image too
#   backdrop render KIND OUT.png WxH SCALE   one image to a file (KIND wall|lock),
#                        for looking at a layout without touching the session
#
# The wallpaper is Base, or the user's own image scaled until it covers the
# output. On it: the ravnix mark in the middle, the phyllon mark top left at the
# same size, both in the accent; the fastfetch facts with the NixOS logo (in
# Blue and Sapphire) top right; and, when the user lists any, their tool logos
# in Surface grays, spread around the rest. The NixOS logo is fastfetch's own
# and is made of block glyphs by design: it is drawn as the terminal shows it,
# not redrawn as a vector. The lock image is Base (or the same
# image) and the ravnix mark alone, sized to sit inside swaylock's ring, so
# nothing about the machine can be read on a locked screen. It never runs
# fastfetch and never draws a logo.
#
# Until the ravnix mark ships (assets/ravnix-mark.svg), the wordmark "ravnix"
# in the theme's font stands in for it, fitted to the same circle.
#
# Sizes are in logical px and multiplied by the output scale: images are drawn
# at the physical resolution, and swaylock's indicator-radius is logical.
#
# Everything personal or themed comes from one JSON file, which
# modules/desktop/backdrop.nix writes: BACKDROP_CONFIG, else
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/backdrop/config.json.
#   palette  the Catppuccin Mocha colors by name ("#rrggbb"); no color is
#            written in this file
#   accent   the name of the accent in the palette
#   font     the family of the facts and the wordmark
#   image    the user's image (absolute path) or null
#   tools    SVG files of tool logos, in order, or []
#
# Other seams, for tests and for running from a checkout:
#   BACKDROP_ASSETS  the directory of the marks (default: ../../assets of this file)
#   BACKDROP_FACTS   a file holding what fastfetch prints, drawn instead of
#                    running fastfetch
#   BACKDROP_FASTFETCH_SECONDS   how long fastfetch gets (default 10)
#   XDG_CACHE_HOME   where the images are kept (backdrop/ below it)
#
# Whatever is wrong with the image, a logo or the facts, the wallpaper is still
# drawn and the problem is one line on stderr (the journal, under sway). Only a
# broken config, bad arguments or a sway that refuses fail the command.
#
# Called by lock-screen (lock-args, then wallpaper after unlock) and by every
# kanshi profile's exec (wallpaper), which runs at login, on each sway reload
# (kanshi is exec_always) and when a monitor is plugged in or out.

